Isolated local Docker fixture --network none, private system/session buses, no host HOME, display/socket, settings or /opt mount. Separate fixture user uid 1000 and preexisting favorite autobyteus-managed.desktop. No GNOME restart/reload or favorites mutation performed by the app. Only synthetic fixture screenshots.
Built two temp Go drivers: actual native Menu from pre-fix eb5ca25f57; EnsureMenu from 960fb46ad0. Actual 512 PNG generated via the build recipe from the existing SVG (sha256 a62a83956f5fafc8ba766c853b788bc725fb2cd262f0dd98f447e838fb9d4630). Drivers invoked strictly as test user; command registered at canonical path was inert. This is an OS presentation self-check, NOT a protected install/window test.
One running Shell: search AutoByteus with legacy fixture -> inspect dock + result -> leave overview -> invoke corrected native publication -> wait on Shell lookup resolving the nested file -> reopen Applications/search. No manual cache invalidation. Before: blue generic icon in search and dock. Normal live index transition can lag: an already constructed search result still showed predecessor art while the favorite had updated. After registry settled and overview search was entered, one branded green/blue result and the same brand at the unchanged dock favorite. See before/indexing/after PNGs; no running-window association claimed.
